{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Added an `audit_log` table (new migration) and `Storage.AppendAuditLog`; every API request that modifies `users` or `feeds` now appends a row. The build and existing tests pass; the new audit behaviour itself is not covered by any test I could run.\n\nWhere rows are appended:\n- **REST API, users:** create, update, remove.\n- **REST API, feeds:** create, update, remove, single-feed refresh (also when the refresh fails, since the error counter is written), OPML import, and category removal when it cascades to feeds.\n- **Google Reader API:** quick-add, subscribe, unsubscribe, rename, move, and disable-tag (which moves feeds to another category).\n- **Not audited:** the last-login update in the API, Fever and Google Reader auth paths, as the task specifies. UI, CLI and background worker writes are also untouched.\n\nThings to know:\n- **Schema is my own design.** Columns are `id`, `created_at`, `user_id` (the requesting user, no foreign key so rows survive user deletion), `table_name`, `action`, `row_id` (0 when several rows are affected).\n- **Not transactional.** The audit row is inserted right after the write, not in the same transaction; if the insert fails the request returns a server error but the original write stands.\n- **Refresh-all and refresh-category are audited too.** These only queue background jobs, so the feed rows are written by the worker later; I append one row when at least one job is queued. Say if you would rather these not count.\n- **Import and category removal are audited by feed count.** A row is appended only if the user's feed count changed, so a rejected or no-op import adds nothing and a partially failed import is still recorded.\n- **Disable-tag over-audits slightly.** It appends a row on success even if the removed categories held no feeds.\n- **Annotations are partly stale.** I added `audit_log` to the `.agentpolicy` nouns for `internal/storage`, `internal/api` and `internal/googlereader`, and updated `@effects` tags on the handlers I changed. The ", "t": 1794462338.643}
